  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<para>Solve this system of equations without graphing. Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>

<para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}5x\;+\;y\;=\;7\\y\;=\;-20x\;+\;2\end{array}\right.\)</para>

<!-- BEGIN TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<!--Q1-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the \(x\) value?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> \(\frac15\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!-- END TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="c07ed19f-0d53-4979-9b9e-a2e7ad64c830" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="1d10d402-b443-4531-bfcf-dc65abd33808" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="6">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the \(y\) value?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 6</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>
<!-- END ACTIVITY INPUT 1 TRY -->
<!-- BEGIN TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<!--Q3-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Explain your solutions.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some samples.</para>
    <list>
      <item>Substituting \( 20x + 2 \) for \( y \) in the first equation, \( 5x+y=7 \), gives \( 5x + (20x+2) = 7 \) or \( 25x + 2 = 7 \), which then gives \( x=\frac15 \). Substituting \( \frac15 \) for \( x \) in the first equation and solving for \( y \) gives \( y=6 \).</item>
      <item>The first equation, \( 5x+y=7 \), can be rearranged to \( y = 7 - 5x \). Substituting \( 7-5x \) for \( y \) in the second equation gives \( 20x + 2 = 7-5x \). Solving this equation leads to \( x=\frac15 \), and substituting \( \frac15 \) for \( x \) in either equation gives \( y=6 \).</item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!-- END TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<div class="os-raise-student-reflection">
  <para class="os-raise-student-reflection-title">Building Character: Growth Mindset</para>
  <div class="os-raise-d-flex-nowrap os-raise-gap-1">
    <image height="200" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/73874f1a255999b5120ed446429bafe1e18ea4c2" width="200px"/>
    <div>
      <para class="os-raise-mb-0">Having a growth mindset means believing you can improve your abilities. Compared to a fixed mindset, a growth mindset encourages you to embrace challenges, sustain effort, and try new strategies.</para>
      <para>Think about your current sense of having a growth mindset. Are the following statements are true for you?</para>
      <list>
        <item>
          After I make a mistake, I always look for ways to learn from it.
        </item>
        <item>
          I love challenges because they make me smarter.
        </item>
      </list>
      <para>Don’t worry if none of these statements are true for you. Developing this trait takes time. Your first step starts today!</para>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>
